IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 (Singapore) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- A fact here is one a witness, a document or a finding of the court could
-- give ("she typed the administrator's password into the payroll server");
-- whether that is "access without authority" is a rule (s 2(5)).
--
-- Source: ../source/CMA1993.txt (SSO PDF, current version as at 07 Oct 2026).

§ `Computer Misuse Act 1993 — the nouns`

§§ `The device (s 2(1) "computer")`

-- s 2(1) "computer" ... "but does not include —"
DECLARE `Device exclusion` IS ONE OF
    `not excluded`
    `(a) an automated typewriter or typesetter`
    `(b) a portable hand-held calculator`
    `(c) a similar device which is non-programmable or has no data storage facility`
    `(d) a device the Minister has prescribed by Gazette notification`

DECLARE Device HAS
    `is an electronic, magnetic, optical, electrochemical or other data processing device, or a group of them`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `performs logical, arithmetic or storage functions`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion`                                          IS A `Device exclusion`

§§ `What the act did to programs or data (s 2(2)-(4), (7))`

-- s 2(2): what the function the person caused the computer to perform did.
DECLARE `Effect on programs or data` HAS
    `altered or erased the program or data`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(2)(a), 2(7)(a)
    `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 2(2)(b)
    `used the data`                                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(2)(c)
    `caused the program to be executed`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(3)(a)
    `was itself a function of the program`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(3)(b)
    `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 2(2)(d), 2(4)
    `added a program or data to the computer's contents` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(7)(b)
    `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 2(7)(c)

-- s 2(5) and (8): who may control the access, or decide the modification.
DECLARE Authority HAS
    `the person is entitled to control (or determine) access or modification of the kind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has consent from a person so entitled`   IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Damage (s 2(1) "damage")`

-- s 2(1) "damage" — except for the purposes of s 17.
DECLARE `Impairment facts` HAS
    `an impairment to a computer or to the integrity or availability of data, a program, a system or information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `loss caused, in dollars, within one year after the offence`   IS A NUMBER   -- (a): later loss "must not be taken into account"
    `a different loss threshold prescribed by the Minister`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `modifies or impairs, or potentially, medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `causes or threatens physical injury or death`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `threatens public health or public safety`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d)

§§ `The protected computer (s 11)`

-- s 11(2): what the computer, program or data is "used directly in
-- connection with or necessary for".
DECLARE `Protected use` IS ONE OF
    `none of the s 11(2) uses`
    `(a) the security, defence or international relations of Singapore`
    `(b) the existence or identity of a confidential source of criminal law enforcement information`
    `(c) communications infrastructure, banking and financial services, public utilities, public transportation or public key infrastructure`
    `(d) the protection of public safety, including essential emergency services`

DECLARE `Protected computer facts` HAS
    `access to the computer was obtained in the course of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `use`                                                    IS A `Protected use`
    `the accused knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a warning of the enhanced penalty was exhibited to the accused`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(3)
    `the contrary of the presumed knowledge is proved`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 11(3) "until the contrary is proved"

§§ `The offences (Part 2)`

-- s 4(2): the offence the accused intended.
DECLARE `Intended offence` HAS
    `involves property, fraud or dishonesty, or causes bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment on conviction, in years`           IS A NUMBER

-- s 8A(3): the facts that raise the presumption of reasonable grounds.
DECLARE `s 8A presumption facts` HAS
    `did the act for any gain, wrongful or not, realised or not, to anyone` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `did it knowing it is likely to cause wrongful loss`     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `failed to take reasonable steps to ascertain the identity and physical location of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN -- (c)
    `the contrary is proved`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- "until the contrary is proved"

-- ss 8A(5), 8B(5A)-(5B): the scam facts behind caning.
DECLARE `Scam facts` HAS
    `knew the purpose or use was a scam offence`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- 8A(5)(a), 8B(5B)(a)
    `obtained or retained it for a scam offence, or for supply for one` IS A BOOLEAN -- 8B(5A)
    `proved to the court it was used for a scam offence`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- 8A(5)(b)(i), 8B(5B)(b)(i)
    `the accused proved reasonable steps against its use for a scam offence` IS A BOOLEAN -- (b)(ii)

-- ss 8B, 9: the two limbs, obtaining or retaining, and supplying.
DECLARE `Dealing` IS ONE OF
    `(a) obtains or retains`
    `(b) supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available`

-- ss 8B(2)-(4), 9(2)-(4): the purposes and knowledge behind a dealing.
DECLARE `Dealing facts` HAS
    `dealing`                                                IS A `Dealing`
    `purpose: use in committing or facilitating an offence`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (2)(a)
    `purpose: supply or making available for use in an offence` IS A BOOLEAN -- (2)(b)
    `knew or had reason to believe it will be or is likely to be used for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN -- (3)(b)
    `merely provides network access, routing or connection services` IS A BOOLEAN -- (4)

DECLARE `Alleged offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` HAS
        `knowingly caused a computer to perform a function`  IS A BOOLEAN
        `for the purpose of securing access to a program or data` IS A BOOLEAN
        `effect`                                             IS AN `Effect on programs or data`
        `authority`                                          IS AN Authority
    `s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` HAS
        `caused a computer to perform a function to secure access` IS A BOOLEAN
        `effect`                                             IS AN `Effect on programs or data`
        `intended offence`                                   IS A MAYBE `Intended offence`
    `s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` HAS
        `did an act knowing it will cause a modification`    IS A BOOLEAN
        `effect`                                             IS AN `Effect on programs or data`
        `authority`                                          IS AN Authority
    `s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` HAS
        `knowingly`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
        `(a) secured access without authority to obtain a computer service` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(b) intercepted a function without authority by a device` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(c) used a computer or device to commit (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 7 unauthorised obstruction of use of computer` HAS
        `knowingly and without authority or lawful excuse`   IS A BOOLEAN
        `(a) interfered with, interrupted or obstructed lawful use` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(b) impeded access to, or impaired, a program or data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 8 unauthorised disclosure of access code` HAS
        `knowingly and without authority disclosed a means of access` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(a) for wrongful gain`                              IS A BOOLEAN
        `(b) for an unlawful purpose`                        IS A BOOLEAN
        `(c) knowing it is likely to cause wrongful loss`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` HAS
        `is a user of the national digital identity service` IS A BOOLEAN
        `disclosed own password or access code, or provided other means of access` IS A BOOLEAN
        `knew or had reasonable grounds to believe the purpose was an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
        `presumption`                                        IS AN `s 8A presumption facts`
        `had reasonable grounds to believe it was for a lawful transaction in own identity` IS A BOOLEAN -- (4)
        `scam`                                               IS A `Scam facts`
    `s 8B dealing in another person's credential` HAS
        `the thing is another person's password, access code, biometric identifier or registered application` IS A BOOLEAN
        `facts`                                              IS A `Dealing facts`
        `scam`                                               IS A `Scam facts`
    `s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` HAS
        `knew or had reason to believe it was obtained in contravention of s 3, 4, 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is information about an individual of a type commonly used to identify one` IS A BOOLEAN
        `facts`                                              IS A `Dealing facts`
    `s 10 obtaining items for use in certain offences` HAS
        `the item is a device or program for, or a password or access code to, a computer` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(a)(i) obtained or retained it intending to commit an offence under ss 3-7` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(a)(ii) obtained or retained it with a view to its supply for such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
        `(b) made or supplied it intending it to be used for such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12(1): "abets ... attempts to commit or does any act preparatory to or in
-- furtherance of the commission of any offence under this Act".
DECLARE Participation IS ONE OF
    `as principal`
    `by abetment`
    `by attempt`
    `by a preparatory act or an act in furtherance`

§§ `Punishment`

-- What a court may impose, at most: a fine in dollars, imprisonment in years,
-- strokes of the cane.
DECLARE `CMA punishment` HAS
    `fine`                     IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment in years`    IS A NUMBER
    `caning strokes`           IS A NUMBER

§§ `Territorial scope (s 13)`

-- s 13(4): "serious harm in Singapore".
DECLARE `Serious harm` IS ONE OF
    `no serious harm in Singapore`
    `(a) illness, injury or death of individuals in Singapore`
    `(b) disruption of, or serious diminution of confidence in, an essential service in Singapore`
    `(c) disruption of, or serious diminution of confidence in, the Government, an Organ of State or a statutory board`
    `(d) damage to the national security, defence or foreign relations of Singapore`

DECLARE `Territorial facts` HAS
    `the accused was in Singapore at the material time`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 13(3)(a)
    `the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the material time` IS A BOOLEAN -- (b)
    `harm caused or significantly risked`                         IS A `Serious harm` -- (c)

§§ `The case`

DECLARE Case HAS
    `conduct on`                       IS A DATE
    `alleged`                          IS AN `Alleged offence`
    `participation`                    IS A Participation
    `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender is an individual`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `damage`                           IS AN `Impairment facts`
    `protected computer`               IS A `Protected computer facts`
    `territory`                        IS A `Territorial facts`
    `prescribed as compoundable`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16(2): by regulations, an input
